    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Casting Syphon Flesh with only 5 mana available (Vivid Marsh, Orzhov Basilica, Swamp, Forest, and the Forest that needs to tap) costs 4B. The player has exactly 5 mana to cast it. However, this is turn 5 and the player hasn't played their land for the turn yet (Plains is in hand). They should play Plains first before casting spells. More importantly, Harmonize would be a much better play here - it draws 3 cards for 2GG, helping find more lands and develop. Syphon Flesh forces each opponent to sacrifice a creature, but looking at the board: Haiku Gramps has no creatures, Sonnet Valley has only Fain, the Broker, and Gem25F Analyst has no creatures. So Syphon Flesh will only get 1 sacrifice (from Sonnet Valley) and create only 1 Zombie token, which is poor value for a 5-mana spell. Harmonize drawing 3 cards is significantly better when only one opponent even has a creature to sacrifice.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Syphon Flesh for 4B, forcing each opponent to sacrifice a creature when only one opponent (Sonnet Valley) has a creature on board.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains first, then cast Harmonize for 2GG to draw 3 cards and develop toward casting Teneb, the Harvester. Syphon Flesh getting only 1 sacrifice is poor value compared to drawing 3 cards.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 96,
      "player": "Gem3F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 81,
    },
