    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Casting Murder on Fain, the Broker is a questionable use of premium removal in a 4-player game. Fain is a 3/3 that requires mana and sacrifices to generate value, and Sonnet Valley only has 4 lands with limited mana available. More importantly, Murder is cast as a sorcery-speed play during the precombat main phase, giving up the ability to hold it as instant-speed interaction for a more threatening target later. The player should be developing their own board with Whirler Rogue (which creates two Thopter tokens, synergizes with Military Intelligence for card draw when attacking with 2+ creatures, and can make creatures unblockable with Anowon's mill/draw strategy). Spending Murder proactively on a modest threat while forgoing board development that enables the deck's card advantage engine is a significant misallocation of resources.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Murder targeting Fain, the Broker during precombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Cast Whirler Rogue to create two Thopter tokens, enabling Military Intelligence draws on attacks and setting up the Rogue/unblockable synergy. Hold Murder for a more impactful threat or use it at instant speed on an opponent's turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
