      "player": "Gem25F Analyst",
      "decision_index": 115,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 6 lands (Vivid Marsh, Orzhov Basilica, Swamp, Forest, Forest, and an unplayed Plains in hand), the player should play the Plains from hand before casting Harmonize. Playing the land first costs nothing and ensures they don't miss a land drop. After casting Harmonize with all 4 mana (2GG from the two Forests plus 2 from Orzhov Basilica/Swamp/Vivid Marsh), they would have no mana left and the Plains would remain unplayed this turn. By playing the Plains first, they'd have 7 lands on board, which matters for future turns and for casting expensive spells like Teneb (6 mana) or Hour of Reckoning (7 mana with convoke).",
      "action_taken": "Cast Harmonize without first playing Plains from hand.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains first, then cast Harmonize. This ensures the land drop isn't missed if the 3 drawn cards don't include lands or if there's a reason to play a different land next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
