    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Vengeful Ancestor (3/4 flying with goad ability) arguably provides more immediate board impact than Chameleon Colossus in a multiplayer game. The goad effect forces opponents to attack each other, which synergizes with Vrondiss's enrage theme (goaded creatures dealing 1 damage to their controller) and provides political advantage. Chameleon Colossus is a strong creature with protection from black and pump ability, but it's a ground creature with no evasion and no immediate board impact beyond being a 4/4. Additionally, casting a creature before combat when holding Berserker's Frenzy (a combat trick) is generally fine since Haiku Gramps has no creatures to attack with yet anyway.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Chameleon Colossus (4/4 with protection from black and pump ability)",
      "better_line": "Cast Vengeful Ancestor (3/4 flying with goad trigger) to start pressuring opponents, force attacks between enemies, and synergize with Vrondiss commander strategy",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 128,
      "player": "Haiku Gramps",
      "decision_index": 148,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Berserker's Frenzy can only be cast 'before combat or during combat before blockers are declared' and is meant to manipulate blocking. Casting it in precombat main with no attackers and no combat happening accomplishes absolutely nothing - it's a combat trick that requires creatures attacking to have any effect. The card forces creatures to block or lets you choose how creatures block, but there are no attacking creatures to block. This wastes a card and 3 mana for zero effect. The player should have cast Neverwinter Hydra instead, which with X=0 would die immediately but at least with 4 lands (producing RRGG from Mossfire Valley + Forest + Forest + Mountain) they can't cast it for any meaningful X anyway. However, Berserker's Frenzy is still a complete waste - even if cast at the right timing, there are no creatures attacking to make the blocking manipulation relevant on the player's own turn with no creatures on their board.",
