    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Gideon, Champion of Justice on turn 7 with only 6 lands and a hand full of expensive threats (Angel of Serenity at 7 mana, Teysa at 7 mana, Necropolis Regent at 6 mana, Sunscorch Regent at 5 mana). Gideon is a relatively weak planeswalker in multiplayer - his +1 is slow, his 0 ability makes him vulnerable as a creature, and his -15 ultimate is extremely unlikely to be reached. Meanwhile, Sunscorch Regent at 5 mana next turn would be a much stronger play providing an evasive body that grows and gains life in multiplayer. Gideon will likely just eat attacks and die without providing meaningful value. Additionally, casting Gideon before considering using Bloodthirsty Blade to attach to an opponent's creature (like Monk Realist) could have been worth evaluating, though mana is tight.",
