      "description": "Soul Manipulation allows choosing one or both modes. Gem25F Analyst declined to counter Whirler Rogue, which is a meaningful creature that creates two Thopter tokens on entry and provides unblockable utility. The player has no creatures on board and is behind on board presence. Countering an opponent's creature spell for free (it's already on the stack) is pure upside that was declined. Even if they wanted to also use the graveyard recursion mode, declining the counter mode is a significant loss of value. Whirler Rogue will generate card advantage for its controller and provide evasion, making it a real threat especially with Military Intelligence on the Analyst's board (suggesting they care about attacking).",
