    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Soul Manipulation allows choosing one or both modes. Gem25F Analyst is casting it while Whirler Rogue is on the stack. Whirler Rogue is a strong creature that creates two Thopter tokens on ETB, which would give its controller significant board presence and artifact synergies. Choosing to counter it would be valuable. The player also has Notorious Throng in their graveyard, which could be returned with the second mode. Even just countering the Whirler Rogue alone is a clean 1-for-1 that prevents 3 bodies from entering the battlefield. Instead, the player chose Cancel (selecting no modes), effectively wasting the 3 mana spent to cast Soul Manipulation for nothing.",
