    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With 5 lands and no combat tricks that benefit from pre-combat casting, playing Chameleon Colossus before combat means it can't attack this turn (summoning sickness). Vengeful Ancestor (2RR) could also be cast for the same mana and would goad a creature on ETB, providing immediate value even without attacking. More importantly, casting a creature before combat when you have no attacks anyway is fine, but the choice between Colossus and Vengeful Ancestor is worth considering - Vengeful Ancestor's ETB goad provides immediate board impact and its attack trigger would goad again next turn, while Colossus is a vanilla 4/4 with protection from black and a pump ability that requires 4 mana (2GG) to use.",
